# Setup E2E Runbook — @@APP_NAME@@ Project Overlay

> Load the **global** `setup-e2e-runbook` skill first for the full workflow.
> This file records `@@APP_NAME@@`-specific paths and the existing test-book state.

For dispatched runbook work, follow global `e2e-cockpit`'s receipt/status/question
and ACK contract: FIFO/tick only, `accept-dispatch` with `accepted` /
`start_work=true` (sequence 1; dispatch 0 has no heartbeat), then `heartbeat`
running sequence 2. Use `ask` / `access-prompt` with private typed body refs for
ambiguous expected behavior; `pending` / `read-question` return mission-status
JSON. Only explicit human replies; `hold --answers` never approves. Inspect
`status.pending_commands` / `command-status`; accepted-worker cancel/replace
needs accepted then applied ACK with matching digest and typed `--result`.
Reuse IDs/digests, journal no secrets, and separate lifecycle from pane diagnosis.
No raw `send`/`nudge` mission, approval or cancel shortcuts.

If the parent repo has `graphify-out/graph.json` and `graphify` is available,
query it first for feature domains, routes, navigation, API groups, and
user-facing workflows before broad text search. Confirm generated chapters and
specs against source files and `test-book/SUMMARY.md`.

